From 9769ca04e089a3dbe3d02cd84c3743af05c78732 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "erik.hauan" <erik.hauan@radiantvs.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:56:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] engine-manager: slot capacity and jit_load in ModelsResult
 behind E11

Behaviour: the engine:models sweep runs each engine's optional slots action
(a record spec; array-shaped once, query-shaped once per loaded model) after
its loaded_models query succeeds, publishes the capacity as SlotsByEngine,
applies node-settings overrides and resolves JITLoadByEngine for every
reporting engine; list/loaded extraction expands per-instance rows
(spec.Each). classifyRow (matchRow with an "unclassifiable" result, JSON null
included) serves the slots extraction and exclusive.go's residency check.

Seams used: E11 (models.go: ModelsResult embeds LocalModelsExt; one-line
nil-safe sweep hooks newLocalSlotSweep/prepare/collect/finish in
ModelsResult, and expandInstances in extractStringsResult, each marked
// fork:E11; bodies, querySlots, the record extractors and classifyRow in
services/nvpair-engine-manager/local_models.go). NVIDIA's #195 idioms are
kept (wg.Go closure, slices.Contains in matchRow); the moved code uses
strings.SplitSeq, maps.Clone and slices.Collect.

Proving tests: TestE11_Nil, TestLocalModelsResultJSONKeys, TestExtractRecords,
TestBundledSlotsQueryThroughManifests, TestApplySettingsOverrides
(nvpair-engine-manager).

Feature-group commit for catch-up step 3, exported as
local/patches/003-engine-models-slots.patch. It touches only upstream files
and new files so it replays onto NVIDIA; fork-test fallout and records follow
in the fix-up commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
